---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Middle Tennessee Real Estate Guides"
  description="Practical, locally informed guides for buying, selling, financing, and moving in Nashville and Middle Tennessee."
>
  <section class="guide-hero">
    <div class="container hero-inner">
      <span class="eyebrow">Guides</span>
      <h1>Clear context for the decisions behind the numbers.</h1>
      <p>Plain-English market notes, transaction examples, and Middle Tennessee guidance—without the sales pitch.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <span class="eyebrow">Latest</span>
        <h2>What I’m seeing right now</h2>
      </div>

      <div class="guide-list">
        <article class="guide-card">
          <div class="card-copy">
            <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-08-26">August 26, 2026</time> · Homeowner guide</p>
            <h3><a href="/guides/nashville-home-equity-options/">Nashville Homeowners May Have More Options Than They Think</a></h3>
            <p>Mortgage rates can make moving feel like a nonstarter. Record homeowner equity may give some Nashville owners more flexibility than the rate alone suggests.</p>
            <a class="read-more" href="/guides/nashville-home-equity-options/">Read the homeowner guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="card-signal" aria-label="Home equity signals">
            <span>$18T mortgage-holder equity</span>
            <span>$11.7T classified as tappable</span>
            <span>100,820 high-equity Nashville homes</span>
            <strong>More flexibility</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="guide-card">
          <div class="card-copy">
            <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-08-25">August 25, 2026</time> · Market guide</p>
            <h3><a href="/guides/could-nashville-housing-market-crash/">Could Nashville’s Housing Standoff Turn Into a Crash?</a></h3>
            <p>Florida and Las Vegas share pieces of Nashville’s post-boom setup. The differences show which warning signs matter—and what would have to change before “slow” becomes “crash.”</p>
            <a class="read-more" href="/guides/could-nashville-housing-market-crash/">Read the market guide <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="card-signal" aria-label="Nashville crash-risk signals">
            <span>+9% inventory</span>
            <span>−4.2% pendings</span>
            <span>−0.9% median price</span>
            <strong>Watch forced selling</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="guide-card">
          <div class="card-copy">
            <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-08-24">August 24, 2026</time> · Market note</p>
            <h3><a href="/guides/nashville-contract-pipeline-weaker/">Nashville’s Contract Pipeline Is Getting Weaker.</a></h3>
            <p>Detached-house contracts under $300,000 are down at least 21% from each of the past three years. Here’s why that leading signal matters more than the latest closing data.</p>
            <a class="read-more" href="/guides/nashville-contract-pipeline-weaker/">Read the market note <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="card-signal" aria-label="Latest contract signals">
            <span>154 under contract</span>
            <span>−22.2% vs 2025</span>
            <span>Six-week negative run</span>
            <strong>Pipeline weakening</strong>
          </div>
        </article>

        <article class="guide-card">
          <div class="card-copy">
            <p class="meta"><time datetime="2026-08-21">August 21, 2026</time> · Market note</p>
            <h3><a href="/guides/why-the-market-feels-stuck/">The Market Isn’t Crashing. It’s Stuck.</a></h3>
            <p>More inventory, longer days on market, fewer contracts—and prices that still are not falling very much. Here’s why Greater Nashville looks more like a bid/ask standoff than a classic housing crash.</p>
            <a class="read-more" href="/guides/why-the-market-feels-stuck/">Read the market note <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
          </div>
          <div class="card-signal" aria-label="Market pattern">
            <span>More inventory</span>
            <span>Longer DOM</span>
            <span>Fewer pendings</span>
            <strong>Sticky prices</strong>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .guide-hero { padding: clamp(5rem, 10vw, 8rem) 0; background: var(--mist); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .hero-inner { max-width: 920px; margin-left: max(1rem, calc((100% - var(--content)) / 2)); }
  .guide-hero h1 { max-width: 15ch; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }
  .guide-hero p { max-width: 650px; margin: 0; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.15rem; }
  .guide-card { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.5fr) minmax(250px, .65fr); border: 1px solid var(--line); background: white; }
  .guide-list { display: grid; gap: 2rem; }
  .card-copy { padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 4rem); }
  .meta { margin-bottom: .9rem; color: var(--muted); font-size: .78rem; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: .06em; text-transform: uppercase; }
  .card-copy h3 { max-width: 18ch; margin-bottom: 1rem; font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.25rem); }
  .card-copy h3 a { text-decoration: none; }
  .card-copy > p:not(.meta) { max-width: 64ch; color: var(--muted); font-size: 1.05rem; }
  .read-more { display: inline-flex; gap: .5rem; margin-top: 1rem; font-weight: 700; text-decoration: none; }
  .read-more:hover { text-decoration: underline; }
  .card-signal { display: grid; align-content: center; gap: .35rem; padding: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 3.5rem); background: var(--navy-950); color: rgba(255,255,255,.66); }
  .card-signal span, .card-signal strong { display: block; padding: .7rem 0; border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.13); }
  .card-signal strong { border-bottom: 0; color: white; font-size: 1.3rem; font-weight: 500; }
  @media (max-width: 760px) {
    .hero-inner { margin-inline: auto; }
    .guide-card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
